<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Segovesus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">legendary, c. 600 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Segovesus was a legendary Gallic leader, nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambigatus">Ambigatus</a> of the Bituriges. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellovesus">Bellovesus</a> led Celtic migrants into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> around 600 BCE, Segovesus was sent by lot to lead another migration east into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hercynian-forest">Hercynian Forest</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The story reflects Roman ideas about the Celtic expansion.</p></div>
